title: 'M1.6 slice 2 r2 reading: meter time and trust'
summary: A turn counts under its own budget.usage row's at (row written first; FuseLog may return {at}), so runtime and restore agree even across midnight. Restore runs before daemon.start, so its today is the day of the chain's last event; counters are keyed by each row's own day. Chain times beyond wall + 5 min clamp to the wall clock, reported once as a daemon callback event (no log kind, no clientApiId move). Restore counts only kernel-principal rows signed by a kernel key, and usage whose user equals the grant's user.
